      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oldsaybrookct.gov/159/Our-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Governor Winthrop named the settlement Saye-Brooke in honor of Viscount Seye and Sele and Lord Brooke.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oldsaybrookct.gov/159/Our-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Old Saybrook sits where the Connecticut River meets Long Island Sound, blending historic charm with modern flair.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://ctvisit.com/listings/town-old-saybrook"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "More than one hundred homes in Old Saybrook are designated as having historic significance.",
